WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
Hello everybody, My name is Markiplier and welcome back to The Park.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.220
Now we're going to be going on the Bumper cars,

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:10.800
And I wanted to say this game isn't quite what I thought it would be, I thought when it was-

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.400
Uhhg... When I first got here- Examine device?

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.860
Alright, I'll get back to that thought- woah.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.980
-because apparently this is important.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.500
[""No no no no no... Please no!"]

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.480
["Stop! Stop Doctor! Stop it please!"]

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:35.200
[in-game screaming]

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.340
W-well I can say for some sort of certainty that that was not normal.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:50.160
That was one of those abnormal occurrences and also- what the hell was it?

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.760
Why was I being electro-zapped in a chair?

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:56.560
Okay, so, to finish my thought- I thought this game was gonna be more

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.440
"Open World Exploration"

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.440
And it /kinda/ is. Like I don't wanna knock it, it kinda is.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.340
But also, I'm kinda on a path... Here.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.300
I-I believe I can catch you, I just gotta find out how and why...

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.640
... And also where the hell I am.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:19.540
So, like, what I mean by that is- of course you can go anywhere and I'm pretty sure there's a lot of hidden clues throughout the environment

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.400
-that tell the story in whatever way they can,

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.360
,but when I first heard about this game, I thought it was gonna be like a...

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:31.500
Y-You choose the way you go through it, and you choose the way you unravel the story.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.780
And I'm not saying that's bad!

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:38.120
That's literally a thought that just popped into my head and it probably means absolutely dick-diddly

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.040
so ignore me! ...And why is that one on?

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.080
Markiplier: Callum!
["Callum, where are you?"]

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:44.300
Mmm.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:47.220
How is it getting any power? There isn't exactly a grid up above there...

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.240
Because the way these things work is they get power by touching the

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.280
[loudly] electrified fence on the ceiling.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.560
Oh good! Accident report!

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.700
Another one. Great. [sarcasm]

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.660
[pronounces name] FRANCIS... DEHFREEZNEH.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:06.920
[reads report] "During the transport of bumper cars into the arena, one of the straps attaching the load to the trunk came untied causing a cascade of bumper cars onto Francis...

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.560
...who was standing, directing the driver."

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:10.520
"Francis was crushed by the weight of the car."

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.780
"Francis was killed!"

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:12.580
 

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:19.580
"Duuuuude... D-Dexter claims to have someone at the back of the load undoing the straps, no one else reported seeing anyone..."

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.740
"The sheriff requested that Dexter provide them his urine samples..."

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:27.420
"Double checking of the straps after transit should be mandatory and drug screenings for all drivers..."

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.880
"The local laborers are very superstitious and this hasn't helped"

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.100
so was it Chad?

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:33.900
Chad!

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.280
[crashing noises, suspenseful music]

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:42.660
Heeeeey! Wooaah! Heeeeeey!! Woooaaah!! [Markimoo lets out a very manly scream]

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.240
Oookaaay.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.040
Very peculiar.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.020
Huh.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.620
Awfully, uh... suspicious and odd behavior.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:59.520
["Callum! Where did you go?"] 
Callum! This... car just came out of nowhere and tried to kill me! Come on!

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.140
Stop playing games with me...

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.300
I need you to be serious for one goddamn second!

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.020
Please!

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:06.900
["Callum?"]

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.660
["Caaallluuummm!"] 
Markiplier: CaaaaaaaaaAAAALLUUUUM!

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:09.860
Callum?

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.880
[sound of baby crying]

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:13.600
Hmm... [sounds continue]

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.100
[more baby crying noises]

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:15.940
Mmmhmm.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.600
[It's a matter of public record that I am a failure as a mother]

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:20.580
What?

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:28.000
[Once, when Callum was very small, I left him asleep in the car while I ran an errand. I don't even remember what it was.]

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.700
[When I came back, the Sheriff was standing next to the car, watching my boy through the window.]

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.000
[I didn't like what I saw in his eyes. Judgement.]

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.500
[He wrote me the ticket without saying a word, just the scratch-scratch of his pen on the notepad.]

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.700
[When he gave it to me, our eyes met.]

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:52.000
["I know what you're going through. My daughter, Helen, she... Just get some help"]

00:03:52.500 --> 00:04:00.500
[Help was a bolt of lightning. Help was a thousand volts surging through my veins. Help is agony.]

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:05.600
["I'd rather die," I wanted to scream. "I'd rather you pulled your gun and shot me."]

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.000
[But instead my mouth said, "Yes, Sheriff."]

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.320
Oh, okay. I thought that was Chad over there.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.480
It was just a poster of Chad.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:24.020
Okay so that's very interesting. Why...... What is causing her so much stress in her life?

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:30.640
[reads from paper] "Continually delayed by the incompetence of the builders. The problem is that they're locals and they believe a lot of the rumors about what Old Man Henderson used to do here."

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.100
Markiplier: [loudly] What was it?!

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:37.880
And why call him Old Man Henderson?  That's such a nice name for someone who probably ate people.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:43.980
[continues reading from paper] "They grew up on those tales. Every time a bolt comes loose or a wrench goes missing, those fools are crossing themselves against the black magic."

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:50.460
"Of course, that is why I chose this site over all of the other potential ones. Solomon Island is a nexus for dark energies... [unintelligibly mutters rest of sentence]"

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:53.800
Markiplier: Huuhhh???

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:57.280
Huh??

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:03.640
[reading from paper] "I called in a few favors back in Brooklyn and got someone at the local academy to see if they had any interesting books about local history."

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:08.900
"Turns out they do, and it turns out that Old Man Henderson had some pretty strong connections to the Brooklyn crowd."

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.420
"Perhaps something he wrote will help me find a piece of the plans that I'm missing."

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:13.600
Markiplier: Hang on! One second!

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:14.520
 

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:15.720
Huuuhhh??!

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.840
What the fuck are you talking about the 'Nexus for dark energy--'?

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.920
[loudly] It's a theme park!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.740
What are you doing?!

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.180
Why??

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:25.500
[Scratch-scratch the nose]

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:29.420
Man, is that the guy at the entrance that we were talking to before?

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:31.500
["Mommy is coming, Callum."]

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.780
My God.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.880
Oh, good! That baby's back!

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.520
I was wonderinin

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.060
I was won-der-ninin...

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.300
["Stay where you are!"]

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.800
Why is there a baby crying over there?

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.080
I'll be right with you baby, one second.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.800
[So they are going to close the place down. Doesn't surprise me.]

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.520
Markimoo: You'd think that maybe it's already been closed???

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.160
Oh, back in 1980...

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.080
[reading from document] "After touring the park rides and viewing the startling number of incidents suffered here in the park,

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:06.560
"it is the inspectors opinion that Atlantic Island Park should be shut down until Nathaniel Winter complies with all safety regulations."

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:11.080
"While I understand that there is a sensitive political relationship between Mr. Winter and the Senator,"

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:15.540
"I nevertheless suggest that the political considerations be set aside in condemning Atlantic Island Park..."

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:16.040
(deep breath)

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:21.780
"The rides at first glance appear well constructed and maintained, but the sheer number of incidents at the park during the last few years and during construction..."

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.980
"...led me to believe that there is something wrong..."

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:27.540
"...at the base level of construction and we should close the park and fully investigate these flaws."

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:30.260
Mark: Like the Nexus for the 'dark energies'.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:34.700
[reads from document] "To wit, here is a partial list of the fatalities in the park since opening only two years ago:

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:36.420
"Family of 3 killed..." 
Markiplier: Eugh.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.860
"Fourteen separate incidents of broken bones,"

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:40.200
"three suicides--"

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.200
Markimoo: aathluabd "Suicides."

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:48.200
[Continues reading document] "A child seriously injured from the-- on the escalator, over a dozen children reported missing in the House of Horrors..."

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.300
Ahh. You-- Hang on! Wait a minute.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:51.900
 

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:57.000
Over a dozen. A dozen... m-missing... children...

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.340
...that have not been found yet?

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:01.340
[groan]

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:05.420
And just maaaaybe we'll close down this fuckin' place.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:09.100
A Dozen... OVER a dozen. At least thirteen.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:11.080
KIDS.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.820
MISSING

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.060
Alright, and—

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:17.260
...one report of a drowning. But you know, whatever

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.400
C'est la vie

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.480
C'est la v-- ueugh

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:22.100
Can I decrease the speed ple—

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.300
No, not increase.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.840
Slow it down!

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.160
I can't handle it.
[whispers] My stomach won't take it.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.380
Decrease.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.020
Decrease! ...Okay.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:31.200
Can I get on it now?

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.000
Chad!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.360
Gimme a biiggg hug.

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.360
Oh, boy. Here we go!

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:37.420
 

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:38.540
It's gonna go well.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:40.540
I'll be sure to look out for any... Oh, hi!

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:41.040
What are you—

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:41.540
Hey—

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:42.340
Hang on a second.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:43.780
Whatchu doing over there?

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.200
I saw that!

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:46.660
I saw that

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:52.840
Anyways, this time it's not gonna catch me off guard when a Giant Monstrosity™ leans in from the window...

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.340
Ah... This is nice.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.640
This is the peaceful mountain air that I've always been hoping for.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:58.140
Also...

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.860
...didn't they say we were outside of Brooklyn? Why are— why are there mountains?

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.300
Didn't they say that we were also on an island?

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:06.500
Why are there mountains? (Mark is confused)

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:14.000
["People come into your life for a reason." Dad used to say that before mom ran off. After that, he mostly just drank.]

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.500
Markiplier: What a wise man. (sarcasm intended)

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.300
[Things were different for Don and I.]

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:26.300
[When we met, I was sweeping the floor at Susie's Diner. He came in with some workers, but he didn't try to flirt or cop a feel like the others.]

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.000
[He just ordered a coffee and sat there, watching me.]

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:31.660
Markiplier: Creepy.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.000
[When my shift was over, he offered to walk me home.]

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:41.300
[I don't know how to describe that walk. We talked and laughed and eventually, kissed.]

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:45.400
[It felt like love. It felt like a fairytale.]

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:54.400
[I can't tell you if Callum was made that night, or one of the ones that followed. But I think it has to be that night. That one perfect night.]

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:59.400
[Don and I moved in together but then, well... he died.]

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:04.700
[According to the supervisor, his safety harness failed when he was working on the top of the Ferris Wheel.]

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:06.400
[Don was there one moment,]

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.000
[and then gone.]

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.000
[Sometimes people leave your life for no reason.]

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:17.700
[I was three months pregnant with Callum. Fairytale fucking over.]

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.480
Markiplier: The ferris wheel that you're on right now. (LORAINNE)

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.860
And this is your... son's...favorite theme park. (IS FUCKING)

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.960
The one where his dad died. (TRIGGERED)

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.200
(WELL SHIT)

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.760
(Mark rubs his chin seductively)

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:40.100
I'm gonna hold my speculation until the Giant Monstrosity™ appears out from...

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:40.700
Hello!

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.600
Hi!

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:46.040
Alright, you're not the Giant Monstrosity™ but you look monstrous nonetheless.(SAVAGE)

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:51.600
I'm gonna increase the speed and then leave out, and hopefully this thing just tears itself to the ground.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.440
'Cause I've got some questions....

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:59.000
I've got... Hoo, boy, I've got.. So. Many. Questions.

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:04.300
Because— Okay, first off, exactly what I said... about the story.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:11.000
And second, "dark Nexus for magical energies"...

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.000
(FAKE ASS GRIN)

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.400
I—I dunno, I dun, I dun, I don't know!

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:15.000
I don't know.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:18.000
Okay, so I'm just gonna leave this on.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:25.200
...and hopefully it'll just break itself apart, because... it's probably what it deserves at this point.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:29.000
Okay, goodbye! Goodbye abandoned ferris wheel!

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.900
["Where are you, Callum?"]
Markiplier: What was that sound?

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.900
Oh, there's still a baby over here.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:40.900
Oh!

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.400
Oh, did it- Oh, it flung.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:48.000
Oh, it flung one of the wheel cars. 
["Mommy's coming, Callum!"]

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.000
Yeah.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:53.000
Yup. Meanwhile I'm gonna reminisce about how shitty my life is.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.300
Hello. 
[noise]

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:57.800
Oh. Hi! Oh, okay. Goodbye!

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:03.000
Ookay.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.300
(INTENSE TRIGGER)

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.700
Markiplier: Okay. 
["This isn't a game, Callum!"]

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:12.400
Yeah, Callum! Come on. I'm starting to get angry.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:13.000
["Don't do it, Mommy!"]

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.000
Markiplier: Don't do what?

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.000
["Come to mommy, Callum!"]

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.400
["Don't touch it!"]
Markiplier: Don't touch what?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.700
["Callum!"]
["Mommy, he's watching you!"]

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:27.000
Markiplier: Who? Who's watching me? What am I not touching?

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:34.800
[A lot of people idolize their children. You hear them talking about their kids and just the say they talk... their fucking voices make me want to vomit.]

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:41.000
["My angel likes to read..." and "Little Johnny is so good on the piano..." Fuck those people.]

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.300
MARKIMOO

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:49.300
[You give up nine months of your life carrying them, you traumatize yourself giving birth to them and then you spend the rest of your life as their slave.]

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:57.400
[Wiping asses, mopping up piss, feeding them. Little life sucking monsters who take and take and take until...] (You alright there lady?)

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.500
[We all go insane. Any parent who pretends otherwise is just dishonest.]

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.800
[That's called choice-supportive bias.]

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.200
SHE'S FUCKIN GOIN AT IT!

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:17.500
[I am honest. Callum really grinds my gears. And he owes me everything. Everything.]

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:21.500
[It'd serve the little fuck right if I just abandoned him.]

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:28.000
Markiplier: O-kay. 
["Callum, tell mommy where you are!"]

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.000
Markiplier: Okay, so-
["He's coming, Mommy!"]

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.000
Markiplier: W-Who is? Again, who?

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:37.400
There's some people and I noticed some dude at the ferris wheel, is that who you're talking about?

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:47.400
I've got a ride ticket 'cause-- I'm-I'm-I'm willing to bet that if I came here without this ride ticket it would've been like 'I can't get in without a ticket for some reason.'

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:52.400
But it's green now--
["I always wanted to ride this one, never got around to do it before."]

00:12:54.900 --> 00:13:07.400
Ah, okay. It's-it's your kid's favourite--FAVOURITE--park, there's literally five rides at your kid's favourite park. You never got around to this one. You never got around to one of five.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.000
N-Never? Alright, fine.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:15.000
May- I could understand maybe the kid was too small to ride it, you know-- not tall enough, but

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:17.800
Suspending my disbelief a little bit

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.200
[quietly] Alright, let's get on.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:22.800
That's not the point of this, though. That just irks me a little bit.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.800
It's not the point of the story, though. Not the point of the story.

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:29.000
Oh, hi! Hello, sir! Okay, bye.
["What do you want?"]

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.800
["We need to talk about Callum."]

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.800
What the hell?

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.800
["What do you mean? What have you done to him?"]

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:44.800
["I? That's insulting. You and your boy are everything this place doesn't want - the antithesis of what we stand for."]

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.000
["Where is Callum?"]

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:53.000
["The poor child. He tried so hard to do what he was taught."]

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:58.600
Markiplier: [quietly] Oh, oh hi. ["He even left you a trail of breadcrumbs, but the park is just so hungry."]

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.600
Markiplier: Uh-huh.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:02.600
["Tell me where my son is."]

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:08.500
["The witch has him now, has both of you. No happy ending here. I'm afraid."]

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:12.200
["Just...just leave me alone."]

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:15.900
["Fool. You always were."]

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:18.500
Markiplier:  I-I always were a fool?

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.900
Markiplier: Either I'm hallucinating or the dark energies are starting to get to me.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:23.840
[mock-screams]

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:27.800
Oh, no.
Holy crap!

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:34.400
[uncertain] Okay. That's a little bizarre. That has to do with me being e-lec-tro-cu-ted?

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:42.700
I wanna get off the Mr. Bones Wild Ride. I didn't even read that [referring to sign], what the hell was that?

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:45.200
[crash] Woah-okay.

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:51.000
I can't read those words, they went by too quickly.

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:56.360
[crash] M: WeEeEeEeEe

00:14:56.360 --> 00:15:01.100
Markiplier: Not safe, no joke!
"I can taste your dreams"? What the hell does that mean?

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:07.300
Wah, hey. Oh, God. Well, bye, Callum. [laughs]

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.300
Holy shit.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:19.900
I have no idea. I have no- I have no idea. 
[pause] I have no idea.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:31.400
I have no idea what this game's message or main story is. And I'm not saying that's bad, I'm not saying it's bad. I'm just saying, like, from like what it has shown me, I have no idea.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:33.720
[mutters] What the hell is happening here?

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:41.300
[reading off page on-screen] "It works! The calculations and adjustments worked. The transport and storage mechanisms seem to be flawless. What a wunderbar day!"

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.400
"If only these people knew what they were fueling."

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:46.500
"And so what if a few people leave the park at the end of the day feeling dour?"

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.900
"So what if the children are more scared than excited on the roller coaster?"

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:55.880
"This could be the doorway to immortality, and such doorways open only to those who have the will to find the key."

00:15:55.880 --> 00:16:00.100
[pause] [loudly] WHAT THE FU-U-U-CK.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.860
[calms down] -is going on.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:09.300
'Nexus for dark energies'. Okay, anyway.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:14.200
Markiplier: Sorry, just had to get that out of my system a little bit. Carrying on.
["I can help you, Callum."]

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:19.560
Markiplier: Callum. Where you at, Callum? I can help you, [dat eyebrow raise] apparently.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:25.500
Man, so, okay. So if I was going to take a rational approach to this, lemme, let me just pause real quick-

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.000
-I get to take the flashlight and I get to go into the House of Horrors next-

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:38.000
So let me take a rational approach to this. 'Cause--I--let me suspend my disbelief for a second an-and get past the weird and try to tap into the actual story here, so-

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:42.200
Everybody, hold on. Everybody get out your notepads because this is gonna be complicated.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:58.000
So, Old Man Henderson used to do sumping, something, on this land and it's a lot of land so whatever he did was apparently on a scale to such a large amount that it would have been hard to ignore by anyone- let alone the locals

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:06.200
if there’s something on the scales going on that scared, like, just the locals, you think it would’ve had a further reach than this- which seems like modern society.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:16.100
-but again, push that aside for now. This other guy, Mr. Winter, came here knowing something about the thing that the Old Man Henderson was trying to do...

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:25.300
...with dark energies in this 'Nexus' and so his logical conclusion was to build a theme park. But, a-and that sounds weird but here's why-

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:31.500
in my understanding, it was to draw people in to do something similar to what Old Man Henderson was doing.

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:42.000
But instead of scaring the people, he wanted to absorb the joy that people were having at the theme park and kinda suck it out of them like, like a little filter for all their joy

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:46.800
they're having a good time but then it's getting sucked into the energy portal or some bullshit like that.

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:54.600
So, with all that being said, he's trying to use it to do something such as make himself immortal.

00:17:54.600 --> 00:18:02.000
And, this main character is caught in the crossfire because she came to this park bringing her sadness

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:13.800
and she doesn't have happiness so what she adds to the park is actually negative emotions and negative energy so that's why she is not having a good time right now.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.000
Markiplier: Okay.
["The witch awaits."]

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.200
Markiplier: 'The witch awaits'. I don't know what the hell that means.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:24.000
That is my thought. Because, I try to rationalize these things and apparently the witch awaits and I know that

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:30.000
somehow because I talked to a guy who was sitting, spooning me from behind on the roller-coaster.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.000
Markiplier: ...which was very nice admittedly.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:36.500
[Callum has bruises on his arms, finger marks. Someone has been hurting him!]

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:41.500
[I've asked him, demanded really, to know where he got the marks.]

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:48.000
[But he doesn't want to answer me. Something has scared him into silence. He doesn't dare talk.]

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:56.000
[He's been changing too. Something sinister lurks in the darkness behind his eyes. I catch him staring at me at odd moments.]

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:05.000
[In the night he tosses and turns and cries out words I cannot understand.  When I try to soothe him, he snaps and tries to bite at my fingers.]

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:11.000
[I think he wants to talk to me. I think he wants to tell me.]

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:18.000
[But they are watching him, every minute of the day. They are whispering to him in his sleep, changing him.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.500
[They are taking my baby away from me!]

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:26.000
[I can save him. There will be pain.]

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:32.000
But I love him and in the end he will understand why]

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:36.100
Okay, so... that kinda confirms what I was talking about.

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:39.900
He came to this park and apparently he got possessed by something?

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:43.600
I'm not sure if that's the right word for it in this universe

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:52.100
but, that's my thoughts. So, either this is a distorted version of reality and she's having a rough time, or this is actually...

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:57.100
literally right here. No wait, it's the...

00:19:57.100 --> 00:20:04.100
It's either distorted version of reality or this is l- all in her mind and I'm leaning towards the latter on that one.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:06.900
I don't think that this could be, in any way, actually real.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:08.100
[crash]

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.100
...Okay. (mumbles) {ITS OK MARKIMOO}

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:19.420
[reading screen]

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:21.300
Oh wouldn't you know!

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:30.180
[reading screen]

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:31.300
Mark: Was it an eyeball?

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:43.600
[reading screen]

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.880
Mark: So what does that bring the grand total up to?

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:48.800
Over a dozen plus one now?

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:53.000
How many kids? I guess this isn't exactly a missing kid, this is just... dead.

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:56.000
Fu—

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:57.000
[THIS ISN'T A GAME CALLUM!]

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.640
Mark: I heard that!

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:02.200
I ain't gonna take you! What are you talking about?

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:04.700
[noise] What the fuck was that?

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:08.700
A-ohhh. Blood. Hey. Oh, blood. Oh, trail of blood.

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:11.420
Mark: I should follow!

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:16.720
[Mark making annoyed noises]...maybe if you stopped bitching and did your work—

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:21.800
And by work, I mean push the witch into the oven and I guess that was the whole reason-
[spots blood]

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:24.500
Wooh. [pause]

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:26.500
Hey, stop stip-stepping.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:27.300
[ominous noise/tense music]

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.820
Mark: Hmm, okay.

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:32.700
That's weird.

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:37.580
Is he dead?

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.580
He's not actually dead, is he?

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:41.580
[distant noises of infrastructure]

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:43.700
Oh, okay.

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:44.800
Alright then-

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:46.700
Hello, did you do this?

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:47.300
Did you do it? [silence]

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:49.000
Okay, fine.

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:50.000
Maybe I should-

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.200
Hey, hi, hi Chad! {FUCK YOU GAME YOU SCARED US}

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.400
Oh, really? Oh, okay.

00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:58.000
I-I knew something was up when I couldn't back up.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:58.760
But, uh-

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:02.000
Good thing that was totally not a threat to me in any way.

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:04.100
He almost had me there.

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:06.300
Alright, /Chad/.

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:08.180
You wanna play, Chad?

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:09.540
Huh, Chad?

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:13.300
Is that you stip-stepping, Chad?

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:14.300
[quietly] Huh?

00:22:14.300 --> 00:22:15.300
[quietly] Hello.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:17.980
Okay.

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:19.980
'Take pills'? W-hmm-I- [more unintellible muttering]

00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:25.460
[unintelligible Mark noises] I dunno about—I don't—

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:27.620
Strange bottle of pills, hmm.

00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:30.600
First thing, take it? Hmm, I don't know. Okay, fine.

00:22:32.700 --> 00:22:34.200
Markiplier: T-t-these are mine.

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:36.200
They're mine now.

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:37.800
They're mine.

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:40.200
Just as tasty as I remember.

00:22:40.320 --> 00:22:42.320
Oh, oh, boy.

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:45.900
[repeatedly says 'oh, boy']

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:47.900
Does that say [stumbles over words]

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:49.780
"Destroy reality."

00:22:49.780 --> 00:23:05.540
[reading graffiti]

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:12.060
[unintelligible] I took some strange pills, Callum.

00:23:13.560 --> 00:23:14.280
Oh boy.

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:17.140
Where the heck am I now...

00:23:17.700 --> 00:23:20.440
"Don't believe anything they tell you." Yeah, I wasn't about to start.

00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:21.800
Hello?

00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:23.440
Who is that- What is that?

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:23.940
[distorted amusement park music]

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:29.080
[slowly] I'm sorry.

00:23:30.540 --> 00:23:31.040
Oh boy.

00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:32.540
Oh, where did I just come from?

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:34.800
Ooh, nicely did.

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:36.660
Nicely did!

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:38.040
I like that.

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:39.240
[distorted voice] "Don't leave me here Callum"

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:40.440
Callum!

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:42.140
Dang it, Callum.

00:23:42.920 --> 00:23:43.420
Bam!

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:44.720
Oh those worked.

00:23:46.560 --> 00:23:47.060
Ookay.

00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:48.860
[weird laughing of sorts]

00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:50.960
Callum: Don't touch me!

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:53.260
I—...O-okay.

00:23:53.300 --> 00:23:53.800
Hello!

00:23:55.480 --> 00:24:13.960
[reading screen, getting increasingly confused]

00:24:13.960 --> 00:24:19.160
[still reading, but more maniacally. also with more voice-cracking]

00:24:19.160 --> 00:24:51.200
[maximum passion is being reached. he's really feeling the reading]

00:24:51.200 --> 00:24:59.980
[Overloading the passion, ears begin to bleed around the world]

00:24:59.980 --> 00:25:06.340
Oh you're wel- yes thank you- thank you for the applause. I know, that was definitely worth reading right then and there.

00:25:06.340 --> 00:25:09.040
I'm assuming that was supposed to be gibberish for a reason.

00:25:10.640 --> 00:25:11.620
Callum!

00:25:12.440 --> 00:25:13.000
Callum?

00:25:13.420 --> 00:25:15.680
'Pic-pickled Pickled Punks' Okay.

00:25:16.200 --> 00:25:16.700
Ughh.

00:25:17.160 --> 00:25:18.520
Pickled babies ugh.

00:25:18.520 --> 00:25:19.600
Callum: Mommy I'm scared!

00:25:19.860 --> 00:25:20.740
Okay. Me too.

00:25:21.060 --> 00:25:22.660
I'm also trippin BALLS.

00:25:23.060 --> 00:25:24.260
Okie-dokie then.

00:25:26.820 --> 00:25:27.420
[laboured breathing]

00:25:27.500 --> 00:25:29.020
Oh oh, that's not good.

00:25:29.400 --> 00:25:30.720
That's not good at all!

00:25:30.980 --> 00:25:32.380
Ugh.

00:25:32.380 --> 00:25:39.760
[tense music builds up]

00:25:40.340 --> 00:25:41.620
Okay time for a nap.

00:25:44.080 --> 00:25:44.580
Well!

00:25:46.880 --> 00:25:47.380
Okay.

00:25:48.420 --> 00:25:50.740
Why did I need to take those pills?

00:25:50.840 --> 00:25:56.520
I didn- I didn't actually see myself taking them so, I'm assuming just picking them up made things go wrong.

00:25:57.660 --> 00:26:00.900
So that- that was actually all in her mind.

00:26:00.900 --> 00:26:04.820
So that was an example of what that was and I wanna see what's going on here.

00:26:04.820 --> 00:26:06.360
What the hell was all that?

00:26:07.960 --> 00:26:10.400
Was there really nothing else to that?

00:26:10.400 --> 00:26:12.340
Was there really nothing else to this dead body over here?

00:26:13.260 --> 00:26:15.740
That's still over there for some reason?

00:26:15.740 --> 00:26:17.380
We're not all worried about that?

00:26:17.640 --> 00:26:19.040
[breathing in]

00:26:19.040 --> 00:26:21.580
Alright, off we go then! Why not?

00:26:25.500 --> 00:26:26.600
No kidding!

00:27:14.740 --> 00:27:22.300
Okay. Your narration took a sinister turn as well. Not a hundred percent sure... why?

00:27:22.340 --> 00:27:23.420
Callum: Follow the breadcrumbs

00:27:23.420 --> 00:27:30.220
[mocking] Follow the breadcrumbs. What breadcrumbs? There ain't no breadcrumbs, but I'm gonna be going in there in the next episode.

00:27:31.440 --> 00:27:34.160
This is WILD. This is a wild ride.

00:27:34.240 --> 00:27:41.860
I-I I also want to reiterate. I am NOT bashing this game in any way just because I criticize some of the finer points in the story.

00:27:41.860 --> 00:27:49.640
I'm having a wonderful time. I'm having a fantastic time trying to discern the MiNd BoGgLinG 0-o insanity that is being put in front of me.

00:27:49.640 --> 00:27:55.320
And it is really cool, but I just wanted to point that out so people don't think that I'm being mean to this game.

00:27:55.320 --> 00:28:01.180
I'm b-being playfully bantery to this game, but not mean. No meanness intended, this is actually pretty cool.

00:28:01.180 --> 00:28:05.340
So, Thank you everybody so much for watching! I'll get to the next part very soon~

00:28:05.340 --> 00:28:10.300
And as always, I will see you in the next video.  Buh-bye!

